What was carried over from Min
------------------------------
* the architecture: a single Electron main process that owns windows and tabs,
  a context-isolated renderer, one <webview> per tab, a tab strip plus address
  bar, and a local browsing-history store;
* the interaction model: Ctrl+T / Ctrl+W / Ctrl+L / Ctrl+H, a search-or-address
  bar, a history drawer and a bookmark toggle;
* the visual language: a dark, quiet, content-first window with a compact
  toolbar and no browser chrome beyond what a page needs.

What was NOT carried over (deviation from a literal fork)
---------------------------------------------------------
* Min's TypeScript sources and its build pipeline (esbuild/webpack tasks) are not
  vendored; the shell here is dependency-free CommonJS so the packaged app needs
  no Node modules at runtime.
* Min's task manager, tab groups, reading list, update checker and its dozens of
  third-party dependencies are not included.
* Min's branding, icons, colour palette and strings are not used. Everything the
  user sees says UQAB and lives in this repository.

UQAB additions on top of that architecture
-------------------------------------------
* the Start/Stop session control (FR-27) and the 1 Hz traffic panel (FR-29);
* the hard tunnel gate in main.js: tab requests are cancelled unless the engine
  reports a live session, and the tab session is pinned to the engine's SOCKS5
  port with loopback bypass disabled (FR-26);
* WebRTC non-proxied UDP disabled at the Chromium command-line and per webview;
* the consent flow for clearnet learning (FR-30) and the persona picker (FR-28).

